        ],
        "exact_text": "the line was still clipped to his harness, dragging him down with the falling span.",
        "reason": "The line was anchored to his side's trunk, yet it drags him with the falling span. Mechanics are muddled; if the anchor trunk fell, the line would be slack."
      },
      {
        "family": "causal_logic",
        "severity": "moderate",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S161"
        ],
        "exact_text": "hanging from its anchor on the far side, its near anchors torn loose",
        "reason": "The bridge is torn loose and thrashing, yet Arda crosses it on the line and it falls later. Setup of the bridge state is unclear."
      },
      {
        "family": "state_continuity",
        "severity": "moderate",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S179",
          "S173"
        ],
        "exact_text": "\"My line,\" he said, looking at his empty harness.",
        "reason": "The line was anchored to a trunk and he unclipped it, so it is unclear it is his harness holding it; earlier it was also carried over his shoulder, not on the harness."
      },
      {
        "family": "spatial_consistency",
        "severity": "moderate",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S159"
        ],
        "exact_text": "They hurried back toward the bridge.",
        "reason": "Nisa left via the ridge and Arda crossed the bridge to reach the cliff; the camp's location relative to the bridge and returning back across it is unclear."
      },
      {
        "family": "temporal_consistency",
        "severity": "minor",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S080"
        ],
        "exact_text": "I'll be back soon; we want to be out of the corridor before the light fades, and the clouds are already darkening.",
        "reason": "Slightly confused: they are on the island, not in the corridor, and 'clouds darkening' conflicts with sunset-timed ending."
      },
      {
        "family": "canon_integrity",
        "severity": "minor",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S122"
        ],
        "exact_text": "supply lists, wind readings, sketches of these same knots.",
        "reason": "Journal contents lean toward logging detail; and 'we arrived through the corridor' hints at prior-corridor facts beyond brief partial contents."
      },
      {
        "family": "language_naturalness",
        "severity": "minor",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S173"
        ],
        "exact_text": "giving up the rope.",
        "reason": "Redundant tacked-on phrase repeats the prior action; awkward."
      },
      {
        "family": "language_naturalness",
        "severity": "minor",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S058"
        ],
        "exact_text": "Not any pattern he'd ever seen.",
        "reason": "Redundant repetition of the previous sentence."
      },
      {
        "family": "spine_fidelity",
        "severity": "moderate",
        "repair_scope": "LOCAL_REPAIR",
        "span_ids": [
          "S173",
